course: dictionary
lesson: 10462
title: A living fossil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name one special thing, and the words around it tell you what kind of thing it is. «The tuatara looks like a lizard but is the last survivor of an ancient group of reptiles.» Lizard and reptile are clues: a tuatara is an animal, and it is not quite the same as a lizard.
explain: Look at «last survivor». It tells you the tuatara is the only one of its group still alive today. «It lives on cool New Zealand islands and can live over 100 years» tells you where it lives and that it lives a very long time.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: a lizard-like reptile that lives only in New Zealand still makes sense. Context gave you the answer, so you did not need a dictionary.
fact: A tuatara is a lizard-like reptile found only in New Zealand.
fact: «Tuatara» comes from Maori and means "peaks on the back".
fact: The tuatara is the last living member of a very old group of reptiles that lived alongside the dinosaurs.
fact: A "living fossil" is a living thing whose very old kind has survived until today.
fact: «Ancient» means very old, so an ancient group of reptiles is a very old group.
exercise: «The tuatara looks like a lizard but is the last survivor of an ancient group of reptiles.» What is a tuatara most like? | *A lizard-like reptile | A bird that cannot fly | A kind of fish | A type of dinosaur
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that means very old. | reptiles | lizard | *ancient | survivor
exercise: What does the Maori name tuatara mean? | A lizard that can fly | Last one alive | Cool island | *Peaks on the back
test: «The tuatara lives on cool New Zealand islands and can live over 100 years.» Where does a tuatara live? | On the dinosaurs' farm | In a desert far away | In the deep sea | *On New Zealand islands
test: Ben says a living fossil must be made of stone. What is the best answer? | A living fossil is a living animal or plant from a very old kind, so Ben is wrong | Ben is right, because fossils are always stone | *Ben is wrong, because the word living means it is still alive | A living fossil is a dinosaur egg
exam: Why is the tuatara called a living fossil? | It is made of stone and found in rocks | It is a dinosaur that is still alive | *It is a living animal from a very old group that has survived until today | It lives in a tuatara sanctuary, which is a kind of rock
